The '''Smoke Dungeon''' is a winding tunnel underneath the [[Kharidian Desert]]. To reach it, players must climb down the [[smokey well]]. It is visited during the [[Desert Treasure I]] quest to obtain the [[smoke diamond]] from [[Fareed]]. Progressing the quest up until constructing the [[mystical mirror]]s is required to be able to enter the dungeon.

While in the dungeon, the player must wear a [[facemask]], [[Slayer helmet]], or [[Slayer helmet (i)]] to protect themselves from the smoke. A [[gas mask]] from the [[Plague City]] quest will also serve as adequate protection from the dungeon's smoke, however the [[dust devil]]s inside the dungeon will still rapidly drain the player's stats despite the gas mask's protection. Remaining in the dungeon without protection will cause players to receive 20 damage every 12 seconds (20 ticks), though this cannot reduce the player's [[Hitpoints]] below 1.

The Smoke Dungeon is one of three locations that contain [[dust devil]]s, which have an exceedingly rare chance to drop the [[dragon chainbody]] or [[dust battlestaff]]. Dust devils can be killed with [[Ranged]], [[Magic]], or attacked using a [[Melee]] weapon such as a [[halberd]]. Weapons such as the aforementioned may prove useful when killing dust devils, as they allow for [[safespot]]s to be used. The area also contains [[fire giant]]s; other monsters that may be found in the dungeon include [[pyrefiend]]s and [[fire elemental]]s.

In the western portion of the dungeon is a multi-combat, task-only area for players to slay dust devils. Players who attempt to kill these dust devils off-task will be stopped by [[Dusty Aliv]]. Dusty Aliv will also stop players from placing a Dwarf multicannon in the task-only area.
